I've always thought L pets were awsome (as long as I could keep them from
the priests I wanted to donate to, anyway), althought they can't hurt
cold-based creatures.  Still, they do rock!  Well, my latest Master Lich
*is* rock.  I made it to Medusa, and was using cone of cold (the explody
kind) to cross the water, when I discovered a trap door on one of the
islands (surprise!).  My Lich was next to me (it's teleporty), and fell
down to below Medusa.  I quickly found my way back up, and of course
brought L along - don't want to leave it alone, it might go feral.  Much
to my surprise, the L attacked Medusa!  And quickly got turned to stone. 
Oops.  So much for *that* pet.

Oh well, next time I'll know better.  This is also the first time I've had
Medusa not notice her reflection in my amulet - I guess I was invisible? 
Does anyone know if a mirror still works if I'm invisible?

Anyway, happy hacking!

